// `NULL` is a value the language has: `compiler/front/sema.orb` resolves the
// name and `compiler/emit/c_backend.orb` maps its type to `void*`, so
// `if items == NULL` builds today. The lowering pass had no answer for it, so
// the name was reported as an unknown identifier -- E2001 on a load of a
// constant -- and the file printed no canonical TIR.
//
// The type it answers is the string the build IR uses for the same value, which
// is how `object` and `result` are reported: the pass names what the rest of the
// compiler calls it rather than inventing a spelling.
import "../../compiler/tir/entry.orb"

fn main() {
    val source = "fn z() {  val n = NULL  }"
    print(compileFrontendSource("fixture", source))
}
